{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Program Files\\\\PowerShell\\\\7\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command \"Get-Content D:\\\\Claude\\\\docs\\\\plans\\\\legion\\\\dispatches\\\\PROTOCOL.md -Raw\"","aggregated_output":"# Lane Execution Protocol — applies to every DISPATCH-01…07 (Nemesis lanes)\n\nYou are one lane of a multi-lane parallel build. Other chats are editing OTHER paths in the same working tree at the same time. Everything here exists to keep lanes from colliding and to make your work sealable by the coordinator.\n\n## Orientation\n\n- Implementation repo: `D:/Claude/tools/skills/nemesis` (a nested git repo — you NEVER run git commands in it or in `D:/Claude`).\n- Task specs live in `D:/Claude/docs/plans/nemesis/NEMESIS-FINAL-IMPLEMENTATION-DISPATCH(3).md`. Find a spec with: grep for `### <TASK-ID> —`. Each spec has **Own** (files you create/edit), **Execute** (steps), **Acceptance**, **Forbidden**, and referenced **SNIP-xx** snippets (§1 of the same file).\n- Sealed context you build against (READ-ONLY): `schemas/`, `lib/contracts/`, `registry/` in the nemesis repo, and `qualification/book-*.json`.\n\n## Per-task loop (TDD, evidence-sealed)\n\n1. Read the task spec fully, including its snippets.\n2. **Red:** write the test first in your lane's test file(s), run `node --test <your test file>` from the nemesis repo root, save output to `qualification/evidence/lanes/<LANE>/<TASK-ID>.red.log`.\n3. Implement within the task's **Own** paths only.\n4. **Green:** re-run, save `<TASK-ID>.green.log`. All other pre-existing tests you touched must stay green.\n5. Append to your lane fragment `qualification/lane-evidence/<LANE>.json`:\n   ```json\n   {\"id\":\"B4-009\",\"status\":\"implemented\",\n    \"test\":{\"path\":\"tests/...\",\"assertion\":\"...\"},\n    \"implementation\":[{\"path\":\"lib/...\",\"symbol\":\"...\"}],\n    \"proof\":{\"red\":\"qualification/evidence/lanes/<LANE>/B4-009.red.log\",\"green\":\".../B4-009.green.log\"}}\n   ```\n   (Create the fragment file `{\"lane\":\"<LANE>\",\"tasks\":[]}` on first use. NEVER write to `qualification/book-*.json` — the coordinator merges fragments.)\n6. If the task cannot be completed without an unavailable external input or an engineering decision beyond its spec, record `{\"id\":\"...\",\"status\":\"blocked\",\"blockers\":[\"<typed, specific>\"]}` and move on. Never improvise semantics.\n\n## Subagent parallelization (inside your lane)\n\n1. Extract each task's `**Depends on:**` line from its spec; build your lane's dependency order.\n2. Tasks whose dependencies are all satisfied (sealed in `book-*.json` as implemented, or completed by you) are READY. Run up to **4 READY tasks concurrently** as subagents — cheap/fast models are correct for these; each subagent receives: the full task spec text, its snippets, this protocol's per-task loop, and its exact Own paths.\n3. Review every subagent's diff and logs yourself before recording its fragment entry — subagent output is untrusted until you verify the red/green evidence is real (actually run the green test yourself if in doubt).\n4. Tasks marked SERIAL in their book's wave table run in wave order within your lane.\n\n## Hard rules\n\n- Touch ONLY: your lane's Own paths (union of your tasks' Own lists), your lane's test files, `qualification/evidence/lanes/<LANE>/`, and `qualification/lane-evidence/<LANE>.json`.\n- NEVER: modify `schemas/`, `lib/contracts/`, `registry/` sealed files, another lane's paths, or `qualification/book-*.json`; run `git add/commit/push`; add npm dependencies; install tools; print or inspect credentials.\n- If a task's spec requires editing a sealed schema, that is a **blocker** (record it) — schema changes are coordinator-level amendments.\n- Run `node --test` only on your own test files, never the whole suite (other lanes are running theirs).\n\n## Done = final report\n\nWhen every task is `implemented` or typed-`blocked`, reply with: lane ID; per-task table (id, status, one-line note); paths created/modified; blocker list; and the single command that re-runs your lane's full test set. Then stop — do not start other lanes' work.\n\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Program Files\\\\PowerShell\\\\7\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command \"Get-Content D:\\\\Claude\\\\docs\\\\plans\\\\legion\\\\dispatches\\\\DISPATCH-04-nemesis-ux-visual.md -Raw\"","aggregated_output":"# DISPATCH-04 — Lane L2: Book 5 UX, trust-safety, visual, accessibility, runtime-quality\n\n**Read first:** `PROTOCOL.md` in this directory — it is binding. Your lane ID is `L2`.\n\n## Mission\n\nImplement the remaining Designer-derived assurance tasks of Nemesis Book 5: UX flow evidence, visual/geometry/contrast determinism, accessibility evidence, trust-safety lenses, and runtime-quality providers, exactly per task spec.\n\n## Tasks (20) — remaining mapped set\n\n```\nwave 2A remainder:  B5-007  B5-008  B5-009  B5-010\nwave 2B remainder:  B5-011  B5-012  B5-013  B5-014  B5-015  B5-016  B5-017  B5-018\nwave 2C remainder:  B5-020\nwave 3 (SERIAL, in order):  B5-021  B5-022\nwave 4A:  B5-023  B5-024  B5-025  B5-026\nwave 4D:  B5-028\n```\n\n(B5-031 INTEGRATE is coordinator-owned — not yours.) Respect wave order across groups: 2A/2B/2C fan out now; 3 runs serially after its dependencies; 4A/4D after 3. Extract exact `Depends on:` edges per PROTOCOL.\n\n## Owned paths\n\n`lib/design/`, `providers/ux/`, `providers/visual/`, `providers/accessibility/`, `providers/trust-safety/`, your test files under `tests/design*`, plus lane evidence paths per PROTOCOL.\n\n## Lane-specific rules\n\n- Deterministic evidence (geometry, semantics, contrast, focus order, state completeness) stays strictly separate from interpretive judgment (hierarchy, craft) — interpretive paths produce candidates for adjudication, never terminal verdicts (plan §15.6).\n- Visual evidence requires real rendered pixels where a task demands them; if no render capability is available for a surface, that cell is a typed capability gap.\n\n## Done\n\nPer PROTOCOL final report. Expected: 20/20 implemented or typed-gapped.\n\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
